<article class="env-lemma" id="0F0W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F0W">Lemma <span data-tag="0F0W">59.95.7</span>.</a> Let $K$ be a field. Let $X$ be an affine scheme of finite type over $K$. Let $E_ a \subset X$ be the set of points $x \in X$ with $\text{trdeg}_ K(\kappa (x)) \leq a$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian torsion sheaf on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$ whose support is contained in $E_ a$. Then $H^ b_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F}) = 0$ for $b > a + \text{cd}(K)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We can write $\mathcal{F} = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathcal{F}_ i$ with $\mathcal{F}_ i$ a torsion abelian sheaf supported on a closed subscheme $Z_ i$ contained in $E_ a$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0F0N" data-tag="0F0N">59.74.5</a>. Then Proposition <a href="/tag/0F0V" data-tag="0F0V">59.95.6</a> gives the desired vanishing for $\mathcal{F}_ i$. Details omitted; hints: first use Proposition <a href="/tag/04CA" data-tag="04CA">59.46.4</a> to write $\mathcal{F}_ i$ as the pushforward of a sheaf on $Z_ i$, use the vanishing for this sheaf on $Z_ i$, and use the Leray spectral sequence for $Z_ i \to Z$ to get the vanishing for $\mathcal{F}_ i$. Finally, we conclude by Theorem <a href="/tag/09YQ" data-tag="09YQ">59.51.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>